.TH AD_PACKAGE 1 "2026-08-21" "ad 2.0" "ad scripts"
.SH NAME
ad_package \- package the project for distribution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_package
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NAME\fR
    ad_package.sh — Create a release tarball with pre-built binaries\fR
\fR
SYNOPSIS\fR
    ad_package.sh [-h|--help]\fR
    ad_package.sh [version]\fR
\fR
DESCRIPTION\fR
    Builds the C binaries (compute, animator-c, postprocess, pace) from\fR
    source, then archives them together with the Perl pipeline, the\fR
    launcher scripts (diffvim, ad_vim.pl, ad_tmux, ad_compare),\fR
    the Vim plugin (plugin/, autoload/, completion/, man/, DiffVim/),\fR
    the tests/tests/examples/, the scripts/, README, CHANGELOG and LICENSE into a\fR
    single distributable .tar.gz.\fR
\fR
    The resulting tarball is written to /tmp/ad-<version>.tar.gz.\fR
\fR
OPTIONS\fR
    -h, --help     Show this help message and exit 0.\fR
    version        Version string to embed in the tarball filename.\fR
                   Defaults to "2.0" if not supplied.\fR
\fR
EXAMPLES\fR
    ad_package.sh\fR
        Build the 2.0 release tarball at /tmp/ad-2.0.tar.gz.\fR
\fR
    ad_package.sh 2.3.1\fR
        Build the 2.3.1 release tarball at /tmp/ad-2.3.1.tar.gz.\fR
\fR
    ad_package.sh --help\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show detailed help and exit
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ad_vim (1)
